  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2209.03 Suspension",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2209.03 Suspension.\n\n(a) Upon showing of just cause that a license be suspended, the commissioner shall suspend such license for a period not to exceed 60 days after a hearing.\n\n(b) Just cause shall include, but is not limited to:\n\n(1) Failure to notify the commissioner of any of the changes set forth pursuant to Saf-C 2209.01 or RSA 106-F:12;\n\n(2) Any acts contrary to state law or these rules; or\n\n(3) Failure to immediately report a felony, observed, or discovered.\n\nSource. #9484 eff 6-19-09; ss by #12513, eff 4-12-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2200.html"
